{
  "name": "dustinedwards-info",
  "private": true,
  "pinning": "VERSION RANGES, and the rule behind the two shapes below. EXACT-PINNED: the toolchain that builds and deploys this Worker, plus the auth runtime. wrangler, vite, @cloudflare/vite-plugin, react-router and @react-router/dev decide what the deployed bundle IS, so a caret on any of them means a deploy nobody can reproduce from the same commit, and the lockfile is not enough: it is the thing a fresh resolve is allowed to move. better-auth is pinned on a different ground, that a minor bump to session handling is a security change arriving as a patch note. CARETED: everything else, because a library that only affects rendered output is covered by the gates that compare renders, and pinning it buys nothing a re-render would not catch. Bump a pin deliberately, in its own commit, with the gates run after it.",
  "type": "module",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=24.14.1"
  },
